    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n4704" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἀλυκτοπέδαι</span></b> , αἱ,
			<div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>A.</b><i>bonds,</i> in pl., <i><span class="en">
				Hes.
				<u>Th.</u>
				521
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				A.R.
				2.1249
			</span></i>: sg., <i><span class="en">
				<u>AP</u>
				5.229
			</span></i> (Paul. Sil.), etc. (<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἀλυκτο-</span>
			prob. =
			<i>unbreakable,</i> cf. Skt. <i>rujáli</i> 'break',
			but taken by late Poets as 
				=
				<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἀλυτο-</span>
			
			<i>indissoluble,</i> cf. Paul. Sil. l. c., <i><span class="en">
				<u>AP</u>
				9.641
			</span></i> (<i><span class="en">
				Agath.
			</span></i>), <i><span class="en">
				Nonn.
				<u>D.</u>
				21.56
			</span></i>.)</div>
